---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | AirbrushDOC"
  description="How AirbrushDOC.com handles your data: newsletter, contact form, comments, cookies, and your rights under GDPR."
>
  <main class="abd-container" style="max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 24px 80px;">
    <nav style="font-size:0.8rem; color:var(--abd-text-muted); margin-bottom:32px;">
      <a href="/" style="color:var(--abd-text-dim); text-decoration:none;">Home</a>
      <span style="margin:0 8px;">›</span>
      <span>Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 style="font-family:var(--abd-font-display);font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,2.6rem);font-weight:800;color:var(--abd-text);margin-bottom:12px;letter-spacing:-0.02em;">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p style="color:var(--abd-text-dim);font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:48px;">Last updated: July 2026</p>

    <div class="pp-content">

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2>Who Is Responsible for Your Data</h2>
        <p>AirbrushDOC.com is run by a single person: Sergej Voronko (the "data controller" in GDPR terms). No company, no team, no data department — if you email about your data, I'm the one who answers.</p>
        <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@airbrushdoc.com">contact@airbrushdoc.com</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2>What I Collect, and Why</h2>
        <h3>Newsletter</h3>
        <p>If you subscribe, your email address (and name, if you give one) is stored with <strong>MailerLite</strong> (MailerLite Limited, Ireland — <a href="https://www.mailerlite.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">their privacy policy</a>). Legal basis: your consent, given by double opt-in. It's used to send you the downloads you signed up for and occasional new-content emails — nothing else. Every email contains an unsubscribe link; unsubscribing removes you from the list.</p>
        <h3>Contact form &amp; email</h3>
        <p>If you use the contact form or email me directly, I receive your name, email address, and message, and use them only to reply. Legal basis: legitimate interest in answering your enquiry. Messages are kept in the mailbox for as long as the conversation is relevant, then deleted.</p>
        <h3>Comments</h3>
        <p>If you post a comment, your <strong>name and comment text</strong> are stored in this site's own comment system (a Cloudflare-hosted database) and shown publicly once approved. Your <strong>email address is never stored</strong> — if you provide one, only an anonymous one-way hash of it is kept, used solely to display your Gravatar avatar. A one-way hash of your IP address is stored briefly for spam and rate-limiting purposes only. Legal basis: your consent, by submitting the comment. You can request removal of any comment you wrote at any time.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section" id="cookies">
        <h2>Cookies &amp; Tracking</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Essential storage:</strong> Your cookie-consent choice is stored in your browser so the banner doesn't reappear. That's required functionality and can't be disabled.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> This site currently runs <strong>no analytics platform</strong> — no Google Analytics, no tracking pixels, no advertising profiles. If privacy-respecting, aggregate-only analytics are added later, this policy will be updated first.</li>
          <li><strong>Affiliate cookies:</strong> When you click an affiliate link (marked <code>/go/...</code>), the destination platform (e.g. Amazon) sets its own cookies to attribute the referral. Those are their cookies under their policies — I have no access to or control over them.</li>
          <li><strong>Embedded content:</strong> A few articles embed YouTube videos, and the newsletter form loads from MailerLite. Those third parties may set their own cookies when the embed loads or you interact with it.</li>
          <li><strong>Avatars:</strong> Comment avatars are loaded from Gravatar (Automattic Inc.) using the anonymous hash described above; your browser's request to Gravatar is subject to <a href="https://automattic.com/privacy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Automattic's privacy policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2>Who Processes Data on My Behalf</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts the site and the comment system, and provides network security. Server logs (including IP addresses) are handled by Cloudflare as part of operating the service.</li>
          <li><strong>MailerLite</strong> — newsletter storage and sending.</li>
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong> — contact form delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>Gravatar (Automattic)</strong> — comment avatars, hash-based lookup only.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>I don't sell, rent, or share your personal data with anyone for marketing purposes. Full stop.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2>How Long Data Is Kept</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> until you unsubscribe.</li>
          <li><strong>Contact messages:</strong> as long as the conversation is live, then deleted.</li>
          <li><strong>Comments:</strong> as long as they're published; deleted on request.</li>
          <li><strong>IP hashes (spam control):</strong> only meaningful for one hour of rate-limiting; not linked to your identity.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2>Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>If you're in the EU/EEA (and honestly, even if you're not — I apply the same standard to everyone), you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> — ask what data I hold about you</li>
          <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — have incorrect data corrected</li>
          <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — have your data deleted (unsubscribe, comment removal, mailbox deletion)</li>
          <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a usable format</li>
          <li><strong>Objection &amp; restriction</strong> — object to or limit specific processing</li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — at any time, without affecting past processing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To exercise any of these, email <a href="mailto:contact@airbrushdoc.com">contact@airbrushdoc.com</a>. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This site is not directed at children under 16 and I do not knowingly collect their data. If you believe a child has submitted personal data, contact me and I'll delete it.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>If the site starts processing data differently (for example, adding analytics), this page will be updated before the change goes live, with the date above revised.</p>
        <p>Affiliate relationships and merchandise terms are covered separately in the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure &amp; Legal</a> page.</p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.pp-section {
  padding: 32px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--abd-border);
}
.pp-section:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.pp-section h2 {
  font-family: var(--abd-font-display);
  font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--abd-text); margin-bottom: 16px;
}
.pp-section h3 {
  font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--abd-text); margin: 20px 0 8px;
}
.pp-section p {
  font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--abd-text-dim);
  line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.pp-section ul {
  list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 12px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;
}
.pp-section li {
  font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--abd-text-dim); line-height: 1.7;
  padding-left: 18px; position: relative;
}
.pp-section li::before {
  content: '→'; position: absolute; left: 0;
  color: var(--abd-orange); font-weight: 700;
}
.pp-section a { color: var(--abd-orange); }
.pp-section code {
  background: var(--abd-surface2); border: 1px solid var(--abd-border);
  border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 6px; font-size: 0.85em;
}
.pp-section strong { color: var(--abd-text-body); }
</style>
